	<string id="st_dev_spectrum_x_name_short">
		<text>Spectrum-X</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_dev_spectrum_x_descr">
		<text>A two-handed artefact spectrometer put together by the Radar-1 engineers from a Veles housing, Western chips and parts of Monolith emitters. The probe-pistol goes in the right hand, the tablet with the screen in the left, a coiled cable between them.

The screen shows every artefact in its radius that the filter profile lets through, with its exact grade. A filter only hides from the screen, the search goes on. The settings are kept in the device itself.

RMB: point the probe and take a reading. MMB short: the next profile, MMB long: the settings menu (Esc or MMB closes it). It runs on batteries like any device: a wide search drains them faster.

While it is in your hands there is no weapon and no bolts: either you take the risk alone or your partner covers you.</text>
	</string>
